+## Sales (schema 3)
+
+- Schema 2 migrates to schema 3 with an empty `sales` collection and a `sale` sequence.
+- Each sale row has an id, ticket, soldAt (normalized UTC instant), dishId, qty,
+  and an `ingredients` snapshot of the scaled recipe quantities at import.
+- Ticket identity spans all rows of a ticket; subsequent files skip imported
+  tickets. The entire file commits together, including sequence changes.
+- Sales consumption uses FEFO and the import instant for ledger `at`, with
+  `sale:<ticket>` as its ref. Theoretical use uses the soldAt day.
